	"boundaries": [
		"All 807 required local checks passed: complete npm run check, full real PostgreSQL suite, and full container suite. These totals include pre-existing regression checks, not 807 new replay tests.",
		"The actual PostgreSQL 18 pg_dump backup is restored through psql into a different disposable local database. Five post-backup operator restrictions are read through the actual GCS adapter against a loopback fixture. No dump or credential material is archived.",
		"The replay helper executes on the Node host against PostgreSQL in Docker. All 79 compiled runtime files and four migrations were separately compared with the tested amd64 image; this is not a deployed recovery-job execution.",
		"Replay refuses open CONNECT privileges and other database sessions, seals SQL grants before external reads, and stays sealed after success, cancellation or ordinary migration grant repair.",
		"Existing and absent key revocations, minimum expiry ceilings, source tombstones, one-year recovery audit expiry, changed-generation receipts and explicit retry after lost batch acknowledgement have executable regressions.",
		"The initial focused run exposed a real isolation defect: backend_type is null for other restricted-role sessions in pg_stat_activity. The check now counts all other target-database backends. The same run exposed a non-paginating GCS fixture selection; tests now select the actual paginated fixture.",
		"The first full container run passed 10 of 11 because an interrupted-migration assertion still expected three rows. Updating that assertion to four yielded 11 of 11 on the same image.",
		"A type-only import was reordered for Biome after the container run. The full repository check passed afterward and comparison confirmed the compiled files still match the image.",
		"The earlier accepted thirty-minute soak remains attached to image sha256:1319a14dd3aa87cd8bbc4f67c523b4c23c0607bca565f517cdd3bdb5172d7291. This replay image has not undergone that sustained soak or hosted qualification.",
		"External journal-writer quiescence, recovery job identity and IAM, post-restore admission/limit/upstream/evidence reconciliation, journal/SQL retention and object reconciliation, and safe reopening remain unfinished.",
		"No Neon PITR, live GCS or IAM, provisioning, purchase, upstream permission, external pilot activity, production approval, commit, push or hosted CI result is established."
	]
